Package: anonyhost
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-flask (>= 2.0), tor, nginx, procps
Recommends: torbrowser-launcher, pkexec | policykit-1
Suggests: php-fpm, nodejs, npm, python3-venv, chromium | chromium-browser | google-chrome-stable
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://www.tca.ac.tz
Description: host a website as a Tor onion service from your own computer
 AnonyHost publishes a website on the Tor network (a .onion address) straight
 from your own PC: no public IP address, domain name, port forwarding or
 rented server is needed. Static sites, PHP, Node.js and Python apps are
 supported.
 .
 It runs its own private Tor and nginx as your normal user, shows a local
 dashboard (files, logs, health checks, one-click deploy) and repairs common
 hosting problems automatically.
 .
 Your website, settings and onion keys live in ~/.local/share/anonyhost and
 are never touched by installing, upgrading or removing this package.
 .
 Because AnonyHost does not use the system tor and nginx services, installing
 the package switches those two services off when they still have their
 default, unmodified configuration (and switches them back on when AnonyHost
 is removed). Create /etc/anonyhost/keep-system-services before installing to
 prevent that.
